  "reconciled_block": "=== RESCUE CAPACITY / TRIAGE (demand\u2013supply gap, single baseline) ===\nBaseline (delay 30, vehicle cutoff 0.7, f=0.3, walk_cut 0.5, N=439):\n  needs-rescuer = 167  =  dispatch-reachable 143 + geometry_unreachable 24\n  capacity model: PoC \u2014 25 min per rescue cycle, window W=75 min, units mobilised at the 30-min dispatch delay.\n  *** capacity is a PoC parameter, NOT measured \uc601\ub355 fire-service capacity ***\n\n=== CAPACITY SWEEP (units \u2208 [1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8]), full N=439 ===\nunits | rescued | deferred | geometry | % demand met | % of reachable met\n  1   |       3 |      140 |       24 |         1.8% |              2.1%\n  2   |       6 |      137 |       24 |         3.6% |              4.2%\n  3   |       9 |      134 |       24 |         5.4% |              6.3%\n  4   |      12 |      131 |       24 |         7.2% |              8.4%\n  6   |      18 |      125 |       24 |        10.8% |             12.6%\n  8   |      24 |      119 |       24 |        14.4% |             16.8%\n\n=== INVARIANTS ===\n  three-way sums to needs-rescuer in every cell           : True\n  unlimited units \u2192 recovers DEADLINE-FEASIBLE dispatch set: True (rescued 80=deadline-feasible 80 of dispatch 143; 63 dispatchable homes have their DIRECT ingress corridor cut before the direct ETA [reachable only via detour]; geometry 24)\n  rescued_in_time monotone increasing with units          : True (3 -> 6 -> 9 -> 12 -> 18 -> 24)\n  capacity binds (1 unit leaves demand unmet)             : True\n  2-D baseline cell reconciles with 1-D + run_pipeline    : True\n\n=== READING ===\n  Geometry alone caps timely rescue at 85.6% of demand (143/167); the rest (24) have no surviving corridor.\n  At the baseline 3 units only 5.4% of demand is met in the window \u2014 the gap is the quantitative case for pre-positioning + triage, not a 'lives saved' figure.\n  Robust result = the SHAPE of the curve (sharp unmet demand at realistic unit counts); the absolute % moves with the PoC service time / window."
